TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"verdict":"retry","diagnosis":"Failed the ownership gate conflict-domains because the attempt left head identical to the prepared base 71f2beba0ecd7358eda99e574e078d081f55bbfa, so no task work existed to validate. Evidence: the captured diff is empty (head == baseRev, empty patch), the driver reported \"spec-build-driver: agent produced no commit relative to the prepared base\", and the worktree is clean with docs/ still holding only GATE0.md and CONTINGENCY-sampler-cu-remaining-1024-launches.patch — no docs/MORNING.md and no docs/ANNOUNCE.md. The accompanying result-projection-timeout on the finalMessage capture is a downstream symptom of the attempt ending without a committed result, not an independent machinery fault, so this is not transient; the missing deliverables are both inside the authorized docs prefix, so it is not blocked either. Attempt 2 steering: (1) read specs/flashnext/spec.md#r6 and #r7, IMPORTS.md, and README.md for style before writing; (2) create docs/MORNING.md carrying the five required sections with those literal headings — \"Receipt review\" (one row per receipt under results/receipts with status and the bound it was graded against), \"Open items\" (every spec UNKNOWN with its drain state), \"Promotion checklist\" (operator verification before any fleet change, per ruling P13), \"Optimization menu\" (tuned mixture-kernel config generation for this GPU, graph-capture matrix, jumbo-frame A-B, draft-length sweep, four-bit expert lane pointers from IMPORTS.md), and a blocker template implementing ruling P16 that uses the word \"blocker\"; (3) create a non-empty docs/ANNOUNCE.md covering the two 128 GB unified-memory desktops, two fast rails, one control wire, what was built overnight, where evidence lives, and where benchmarks land; (4) run the ledger-sections acceptance argv locally and see it pass; (5) git add only paths under docs/, commit, and confirm git status --porcelain prints nothing before finishing. Committing is